panvk: import dma-bufs on a backend that cannot export them (kbase)

- pan_kmod_dev_props.limits.dma_buf_import: with no_fd_sharing, a backend may still import
  dma-bufs as buffer objects (pan_kmod_bo_import()), never export them. False for the DRM
  backends, which share fds both ways.
- PanVK offers VK_KHR_external_memory_fd and VK_EXT_external_memory_dma_buf on such a backend,
  and reports dma-bufs as importable only: not exportable, no opaque fds, images only with
  DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR (an import lives at the GPU VA the backend gave it, not at the 64 KiB
  alignment interleaved 64K images need) (vkGetPhysicalDeviceExternalBufferProperties, the
  external image format properties). Fence and semaphore fds stay off.
- vkAllocateMemory maps a buffer object the backend placed itself (pan_kmod_bo::fixed_va: an
  imported dma-buf on kbase lives at the GPU VA kbase gave it) at that VA instead of one from the
  VA heaps, and vkFreeMemory gives no such VA back to the heaps, as panvk_priv_bo does for
  GPU_SYNC memory. Such a BO lives at that VA, so a non-zero opaque capture address for another
  VA is refused (VK_ERROR_INVALID_OPAQUE_CAPTURE_ADDRESS).
- vkBindImageMemory refuses an interleaved 64K image on such a BO at a VA that is not 64 KiB
  aligned (the import is only page aligned; such imports are not offered).

Mesa's WSI then imports the app's buffers (patches/mesa/0004: vkGetMemoryFdPropertiesKHR, a
dedicated import into a linear image with an explicit row pitch) on kbase as on panthor.

